A||||3||Rodney||Clutch slave speed bleeder kits||||1||
Z||000000||Rodney||09-19-2001||09:42 PM||||There are speed bleeders available for brakes. You<BR>loosen the bleeder and just pump the brakes. No need to<BR>keep tightening the bleeder between pumps as it has a<BR>spring loaded ball check valve. Unfortunately they do<BR>not make one to fit the Fiero clutch slave and they<BR>have no current plans to make one to fit. Wouldn't it<BR>be nice to just open the bleeder and pump until the<BR>clutch system is nicely bled? Quick and easy and fast!<P>My solution is to make an adapter that screws into the<BR>slave where the old bleeder is and use a common size<BR>speed bleeder they do offer.  I have a few prototypes.<BR>List price will be around $21.00 and shipping. Anyone<BR>interested in trying one can have one for $15.00 and<BR>shipping is included. Limited availability on these<BR>prototypes.<P>Thanks,<BR>Rodney Dickman<BR>New web page! <A HREF="http://www.rodneydickman.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.rodneydickman.com</A> <P>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Nashco||09-19-2001||10:17 PM||||Hey, sounds like a good idea Rodney.  Did you try using it with a previously dry line, as if you had installed a new slave or master?  I had trouble bleeding my system when I first did it, until I found Archie's directions.  I found the key is to pump the system a few times, then to *push the slave rod in and use it to bleed the system* as Archie directed me to do.  What kind of pressure do the speed bleeders hold?  Is it low enough you could pump it open with your fingers pushing the slave rod in?<P>Good luck with this, sounds like a cool deal.  They are a cool design, I like them, but I'm too cheap to get them <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000002||Phil||09-19-2001||10:25 PM||||On Lawrence's  electricweb magazine site he has a method of making yur own speed bleeders. Quickly: you get a spare bleeder screw and drill the hole all the way thru then get a valve stem from an old tire( tire stores have piles of them) and attach the valve stem to the modded bleeder screw ( I used a short piece of hose and cable ties) and pump away.||||reg||1
